        "Set discriminant $\\Delta = 6^2 - 8(1 + k) = 0 \\implies k = 3.5 = \\frac{7}{2}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Equate the curve and straight line equations:\n$$2x^2 + 8x + 1 = 2x - k \\implies 2x^2 + 6x + (1 + k) = 0$$",
        "Apply the tangency condition requiring discriminant $\\Delta = 0$:\n$$6^2 - 4(2)(1 + k) = 0 \\implies 36 - 8(1 + k) = 0$$\n$$8(1 + k) = 36 \\implies 1 + k = \\frac{36}{8} = 4.5 \\implies k = 3.5 = \\frac{7}{2}$$"
      ],
